    "https://hr.northeastern.edu/careers/locations/": {
      "title": "Locations",
      "description": "Locations - Human Resources Careers · Job Listings · Locations · Professional Development · Compensation Program · Employee Recognition · Service Recognition Benefits · Health Benefits · Tuition Assistance · Paid Time Off · Wellness & Life · Retirement · Commuting & Transportation Community · Belonging · Learning & Growth · HR Business Partners · Life on and off Campus About · Our Values · HR Leadership Team · HR Service Center · U.S. Workplace Posters · Canada Workplace Posters · Human Resources Privacy of Personal Data · Contact Us Careers Job Listings Locations Professional Development Compensation Program Employee Recognition Service Recognition Benefits Health Benefits Tuition Assistance Paid Time Off Wellness & Life Retirement Commuting & Transportation Community Belonging Learning & Growth HR Business Partners Life on and off Campus About Our Values HR Leadership Team HR Service Center U.S. Workplace Posters Canada Workplace Posters Human Resources Privacy of Personal Data Contact Us Careers Locations Careers Job Listings Locations Professional Development Compensation Program World-class, experience-based learning Our worldwide network is made up of over a dozen university campuses offering unique, distinctive approaches to teaching and research. From tech hubs focused on advancing artificial intelligence to a coastal sustainability campus, Northeastern University is home to experienced, industry-specific faculty and staff. Boston Our founding campus and the heart of our global research enterprise. Boston is a comprehensive hub for learning and discovery in a dynamic, urban community. London European hub for our world-leading Network Science Institute. Offering a highly personalized student experience, with the unique opportunity to earn a U.S./U.K. double degree in four years. Oakland Our 135-acre Bay Area campus and home to the Mills Institute. Education and research are shaped by the region’s vibrant community of entrepreneurship, Big Tech, and social impact. New York City Our residential Manhattan campus with access to NYC’s biggest industries—and the experiential model to make the most of it all. Arlington Our Arlington, Virginia campus is located in the heart of the National Capital Region at the intersection of technology, innovation, policy, and security. Our graduate programs in computer science, public policy, analytics, cybersecurity, and security and intelligence studies prepare learners to lead in the region’s future jobs. Burlington The Innovation Campus at Burlington offers a unique research-partnership model. Faculty and students work closely with experts from industry, government, and academia to develop new technologies, materials, and systems. Charlotte In an area that is a recognized leader in the energy, financial services, and healthcare industries, our Charlotte campus provides a large portfolio of industry-aligned opportunities. This location also regularly hosts on-campus events focused on current global workforce trends. Miami Our Miami campus is in Wynwood, the city ’ s creative and cultural hub. Access unique academic programming designed to help you gain the credentials and skills you need to excel in the region ’ s expanding tech, finance, and health sectors, no matter your academic background. Nahant The Coastal Sustainability Institute is committed to conducting innovative research that creates sustainable solutions to confront challenges for the world’s coastal ecosystem. This coastal-focused location works toward creating cleaner, safer, and smarter coastal communities. Portland The Roux Institute combines industry, academia, and government to set our education and research model apart from the rest. The Portland, Maine, location builds expertise in artificial intelligence, computer and data science, digital engineering, and the advanced life sciences and medicines. Seattle Surrounded by high-profile innovation centers, our Seattle campus is at the crossroads of cutting-edge thought leadership and experiential learning. The student-faculty ratio is low, creating a unique learning environment for both students and faculty. Silicon Valley Northeastern’s unique programs, grounded in experiential learning, are customized to offer students the knowledge and skill sets that Silicon Valley employers need. Toronto As Northeastern’s first international campus, this high-tech hub has degrees tailored to Toronto’s economic needs and features curriculum that’s relevant and up to date with industry trends. Vancouver Critical fields such as cybersecurity, data science, coastal sustainability, artificial intelligence, resilience, and robotics are a few of the industry-focused programs taught by faculty who are renowned in their fields at our Vancouver campus. Human Resources 360 Huntington Ave. Boston, Massachusetts 02115 Careers Job Listings Locations Professional Development Compensation Program Employee Recognition Service Recognition Benefits Health Benefits Tuition Assistance Paid Time Off Wellness & Life Retirement Commuting & Transportation Community Belonging Learning & Growth HR Business Partners Life on and off Campus About Our Values HR Leadership Team HR Service Center U.S. Workplace Posters Canada Workplace Posters Human Resources Privacy of Personal Data Contact Us"
    },
